Test coverage (42 tests across the two XCTest suites):
  - Constants            : the web globalProgress literals (TRICKLE_INITIAL=8, TARGET=80, INTERVAL_MS=120,
                           step fraction 0.15, value bounds 0..100).
  - Trickle reducer      : asymptotic advance (8 -> 18.8), never crosses the ceiling, the min-step floor,
                           the at/above-ceiling no-op, strict monotonicity to the target; clampPercent
                           round+clamp (web Math.round(Math.max(0, Math.min(100, …)))).
  - Stack arithmetic     : increment / decrement-never-negative (web activeCount++ / Math.max(0, −1)).
  - Accessibility        : {{percent}} value interpolation + the composed boundary label.
  - Projection           : loading / loaded(empty) / loaded(content) / failed -> every render phase.
  - Controller           : faithful port of lib/globalProgress.test.ts — activate + initial jump, the
                           concurrent-start stack, the idempotent stop token, the asymptotic trickle, the
                           snap-back to 0, subscribe immediate-replay + unsubscribe, replay-while-active,
                           and snapshot-safe dispatch when a listener unsubscribes mid-publish.
  - Model                : start emits view.opened("SuspenseProgressBoundary") + starts the source + begins
                           a progress consumer while loading; resolving (content) stops the bar; empty/error
                           projection; re-entering loading re-acquires the bar; retry forwards; one-shot
                           stale auto-refresh; stop releases the token + stops the source.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY NOTES (what the native surface reproduces from the web source)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Data model      : lib/globalProgress.ts ported verbatim as GlobalProgressController (singleton via
                    .shared) — activeCount stack, idempotent stop token, asymptotic trickle (8 -> 80 at
                    120 ms, +max(1, remaining*0.15)/tick), subscribe/replay, snap-back. Trickle is stepped
                    by advanceTrickle() so it is deterministically unit-tested (web fake timers).
- Bridge          : SuspenseProgressBoundaryModel holds a GlobalProgressToken for exactly as long as the
                    surface is in its loading phase — the native peer of the web ProgressTrackingFallback
                    mounting start() while Suspense is suspended and unmounting stop() once the lazy child
                    resolves.
- Bar             : SuspenseTopProgressBar is the determinate parity of web TopProgress (width = clamped
                    0..80 %, role=progressbar, aria-label t('global.loading','Loading') + live aria-valuenow
                    percentage, fast width transition dropped under Reduce Motion). The shared TSTopProgress
                    is indeterminate and owned by the component-library prompt, so this surface ships its own
                    determinate, trickle-reflecting bar.
- i18n            : the only source key (TopProgress.tsx t('global.loading')) is carried verbatim; resolves
                    through the P1/S10 facade (SuspenseProgressStrings) with English fallbacks. No literals.
- Predecessors    : P1/S8 state-holder + source seams, P1/S9 tokens, P1/S10 i18n facade, P1/S11 telemetry
                    (view.opened) all honoured (mirrors the 0136 ReloadPrompt shared-surface pattern).

DISCLOSED NATIVE CHOICES (no silent drift): the web component is a pure presentational Suspense wrapper
with no data hooks and (beyond the bar's label) no i18n. Per the P4 shared-surface LEAF CONTRACT this
native surface additionally renders friendly empty / retryable error states (never a blank surface) and the
orthogonal stale/offline freshness chip with a one-shot auto-refresh, plus an accessible percentage value
read-out. Colour map is ADR-006 SEMANTIC, not literal: the web cyan->indigo->emerald bar gradient maps to
accent->statusInfo->statusSuccess.

